<CustomMetadata
  xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
>
    <label>Triggers - Logic inside the trigger</label>
    <protected>true</protected>
    <values>
        <field>Domain__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">ApexTrigger</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>IsEnabled__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:boolean">true</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>Severity__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">Medium</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>Category__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">Maintainability</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>Confidence__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">Medium</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>Threshold__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:double">25</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>Description__c</field>
        <value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >The trigger body contains more code lines than the threshold (comments and blank lines excluded).</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>Rationale__c</field>
        <value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >Logic written directly in a trigger cannot be reused or unit tested in isolation, and grows into hard-to-maintain code.</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>SuggestedAction__c</field>
        <value
      xsi:type="xsd:string"
    >Move the logic to a handler class and keep the trigger as a thin dispatcher.</value>
    </values>
</CustomMetadata>
